              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In 2023, Texas enacted H. B. 1181, requiring certain commercial websites publishing sexually explicit content that is obscene to minors to verify that visitors are 18 or older."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Free Speech Coalition, Inc.",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c2805a93c6082b67e99b64b0f3ebc8e58a79a3a0eb67fa066bb84274381910a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c2805a93c60-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Free Speech Coalition, Inc., the Free Speech Coalition argued that adults have a right to access the covered speech, and that the statute impermissibly hinders them."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Texas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c2805a93c6082b67e99b64b0f3ebc8e58a79a3a0eb67fa066bb84274381910a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c2805a93c60-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Texas contends that only rational\u2011basis review applies to H. B. 1181."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Texas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c2805a93c6082b67e99b64b0f3ebc8e58a79a3a0eb67fa066bb84274381910a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c2805a93c60-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Texas also argues that intermediate scrutiny is too demanding and that only rational\u2011basis review should apply."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Fifth Circuit",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c2805a93c6082b67e99b64b0f3ebc8e58a79a3a0eb67fa066bb84274381910a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c2805a93c60-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Fifth Circuit held that an injunction was not warranted because petitioners were unlikely to succeed on their First Amendment claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "District Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c2805a93c6082b67e99b64b0f3ebc8e58a79a3a0eb67fa066bb84274381910a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c2805a93c60-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The District Court granted petitioners a preliminary injunction after concluding that they were likely to succeed on their claim."
      }
    ],
